WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.410
Put one tiny probe inside a resting axon,

2
00:00:03.460 --> 00:00:05.740
and another just outside it.

3
00:00:05.790 --> 00:00:09.290
The inside reads about
minus 70 millivolts.

4
00:00:09.340 --> 00:00:12.210
So a resting nerve cell
isn't switched off:

5
00:00:12.260 --> 00:00:15.300
there is a charge difference
across its membrane.

6
00:00:15.350 --> 00:00:19.270
And it keeps spending energy,
even though it sends no signal.

7
00:00:19.320 --> 00:00:24.630
Why does a resting nerve cell keep spending
energy when it isn't sending any signal?

8
00:00:24.680 --> 00:00:27.540
In this mission, you'll
take a nerve cell apart:

9
00:00:27.590 --> 00:00:31.530
cell body, dendrites, and one long axon.

10
00:00:31.580 --> 00:00:34.630
Then you'll see how many
axons are wrapped in a fatty,

11
00:00:34.680 --> 00:00:37.430
insulating sheath called myelin.

12
00:00:37.480 --> 00:00:42.550
Your mission: explain why a resting nerve
cell keeps spending energy when it sends

13
00:00:42.600 --> 00:00:43.550
no signal.
